Package: unbraid
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Pablo Saura Sánchez <saurasanchezpablo@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: default-jre (>= 2:1.17), libc6, libx11-6, libxext6, libxrender1, libxtst6, libxi6, libfontconfig1, libfreetype6, libgl1, zlib1g
Recommends: polkitd | policykit-1, libsecret-tools, libnotify-bin
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/TheOlympusCloud/unbraid-linux
Description: split tunneling VPN client: every app its own exit
 unbraid routes each app through its own exit, several at once and across
 providers: a banking app can skip the VPN while a streaming app leaves from
 one country, another app from a second and everything else from a third.
 Tailscale is built in. You bring the VPN: NordVPN, Mullvad, PIA, IVPN,
 ExpressVPN, Proton VPN, Surfshark, Windscribe, AirVPN, or your own WireGuard,
 OpenVPN or Shadowsocks servers.
 .
 The tunnels run in the unbraid-engine system service, built on sing-box.
